2026-10-17, node data
- Client in the Network package no longer speaks HTTP. A WarpnetRouter inside
  it serves the Mastodon endpoints from the paired node and returns Mastodon
  JSON for the existing models; endpoints the node has no counterpart for
  fail with WarpnetRoutingError.unsupported. Status ids carry the tweet's
  author, thread root and retweeter, so a cached timeline still resolves after
  a restart, and LinkHandler carries the node's opaque page cursors.
- Quoted tweets are embedded through a warpnet://status/ link, which
  HTMLString now treats as a status link.
- StreamWatcher polls the node's pushes while the app is active instead of
  opening the Mastodon streaming socket.
- The Network tests were replaced with tests of the Warpnet routing.
- Images with warpnet:// URLs load through a Nuke data loader that asks the
  node, and videos through an AVAssetResourceLoader delegate that downloads
  them to a temporary file first. MediaUI takes its player items from a hook
  the app sets, and fetches shared and saved images through the image pipeline
  instead of URLSession.
- Files without the notice line:
  IceCubesApp.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
- The composer counts the tweet's UTF-8 bytes against the node's 2048-byte
  limit, where Mastodon counted UTF-16 units and a fixed length per URL.
- Profiles no longer show featured tags and familiar followers, which the node
  does not keep.
- The Models and Network packages also declare macOS 14, so the Network tests
  run with swift test on a Mac.

