2026-10-17, Warpnet features
- The favourite button is a reaction: a tap sends the default heart, a long
  press offers the desktop client's eight quick reactions, and the button shows
  the reaction the viewer chose. Status and ReblogStatus carry it as
  myReaction, and Statuses gained a react endpoint.
- The boost button opens a menu to retweet or quote. A quote is posted the way
  the Android client posts one, as a retweet carrying the quoted tweet's id,
  which StatusData now passes as quotedStatusId; the composer no longer pastes
  a link to the quoted status into the text.
- Messages are the node's 1:1 chats: a new Chats endpoint lists them, loads
  and sends messages and deletes them, and the conversation screens use it
  instead of direct-visibility statuses. An open chat refreshes every ten
  seconds. The Message actions on profiles and statuses open the chat with
  that account; chat rows and messages offer copy, delete and reporting the
  account instead of favourite, bookmark and mention.
- Editing the profile saves the display name, bio, website, avatar and header
  on the node; the post defaults, account toggles and free-form fields, which
  a Warpnet profile has no place for, left the screen.
- Files without the notice line:
  IceCubesApp/Resources/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings
- Filters are kept on the node: the filter screens create, change and delete
  filters and keywords through its settings routes, and since the node stores
  filters without applying them, the app matches the active ones against the
  home timeline, threads and notifications itself. Filters can apply to those
  three contexts, the ones the node knows.
- Warpnet states Ice Cubes has no place for: a banner while the paired node is
  unreachable, the view count of a tweet in its detail (a view is recorded
  when a tweet is opened), a banner on accounts bridged from the Fediverse,
  a notice in place of tweets the moderators hid, and a notice in place of
  sponsored tweets, whose content is sold outside the App Store and is not
  offered in the app. Status and ReblogStatus carry viewsCount.
