2026-10-18, node errors
- Errors from the node reach the user. The editor shows any failed post in its
  alert, a failed upload shows its error instead of spinning, and a deleted or
  moderated tweet closes its detail screen the way a 404 did.
- The Post button stays off for empty text and for text over the node's 2 KiB
  limit, since the node refuses both.

2026-10-18, share queue errors
- A shared tweet is dropped with a notification only when the node refuses the
  tweet itself. Errors about the request, such as an expired pairing, keep it
  queued. A post whose answer was lost is dropped as unconfirmed instead of
  being sent again.
